---
layout: layouts/constituent.vto
base: ../

styles:
  - styles/base.css
  - styles/diffuse/page.css
  - styles/vendor/phosphor/bold/style.css
  - styles/vendor/phosphor/fill/style.css

scripts:
  - themes/index.js
---

<header>
  <div>
    <div>
      <a class="diffuse-logo" href="./" style="display: inline-block;">
        {{ await comp.diffuse.logo() }}
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="construct dither-mask" style="margin-top: 0">
      Themes
    </p>
    <p>
      Themes are element compositions and provide a traditional browser web application way of
      using them. In other words, pretty much the whole thing, besides your data, lives inside a single browser tab.
    </p>

    <p>
      <small>
        <strong><i class="ph-fill ph-info"></i></strong>
        Each theme is unique, not just a skin; each one might have a totally different feature set.
      </small>
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="dither-mask filler"></div>
</header>
<main>
  <p>
    TODO
  </p>
</main>
